  (text "SAO++ power select: the switch common feeds the LEDs. Position 1 = badge 3.3 V, position 2 = OFF (pin 2 unconnected), position 3 = coin cell." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5b7dca19-1753-5877-bb85-148841780346"))
  (text "The badge supply and the coin cell sit on separate switch contacts and are never connected to each other." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 41.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c81afb9e-5e76-58ac-8198-239e941b68fc"))
  (text "LED-only board: SDA, SCL, GPIO1 and GPIO2 are not connected, so no series diode is needed on the cell (see docs/standard.md section 3)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5c588cbf-fcea-5b6d-98e0-e10c9310caa5"))
  (text "D1 (the sack's gathered top), D2 (the bank note's medallion), D3 (a glint on the coin): reverse-mount white LEDs on the back, shining through the board." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 139.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d495d315-f3c1-5565-bea5-685166ab11fa"))
  (text "1.3 k each: about 0.45 mA per LED on badge power, about 0.2 mA on a fresh cell (calculated, not measured). The maker used 330 ohm on 3.3 V." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 38.1 143.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c79df356-768e-5034-b95c-f45f4f970b2e"))
